  "cards": [
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Two decisions, both must say local", "items": [
      "The client trusts the local flag plex.tv publishes, and Plex only flags RFC1918 addresses",
      "The server classifies the source address: tailnet traffic arrives as 100.x, so PLEX_LAN_NETWORKS must include 100.64.0.0/10",
      "plex-prefs.sh pushes that value and a 95% played threshold on every deploy"
    ] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "Remote Access off", "items": [
      "Turned on, Plex publishes the home public IP; with a public IP the router hairpins it",
      "A TV on the LAN then reaches Plex from the public address and is billed as remote",
      "It is off in Preferences.xml; nothing in the repo enforces it"
    ] },
    { "dot": "slate", "title": "Not in git", "items": [
      "The /32 routes are a tailscale set flag on the raspi, approved in the admin console",
      "Use tailscale set, never tailscale up, which resets the other flags"
    ] }
  ]
